<urn:atm:triage:finding/ARCH-AI-003>
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-27T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:correctionNote "quality-mgr (2026-07-27): QA-1 for PR #667 (fix/phase-ai-arch-line-ceilings @ 46d2af22). This finding is closed as a metric-definition correction, not a code fix -- crates/atm-daemon/bin_support/daemon_observability.rs is byte-identical to the pre-PR baseline (1302 total lines, confirmed unchanged by arch-qa, req-qa, and quality-mgr independently). Root cause of the original citation: quality-mgr's own phase-end review cited the TOTAL line count (1302), not the PROD (non-test) metric that RULE-003 actually enforces ('active limits: prod<=1000' per .just/check_line_counts.py's own summary). quality-mgr independently ran the repo's actual canonical classifier (lint_common.classify_rust_test_scope + is_code_line -- the literal per-file code path check_line_counts.py executes) directly against this file: prod=852, test=327 -- UNDER the 1000-line ceiling. Two reviewers (arch-qa, req-qa) approximated the non-test count via a naive 'everything before the trailing #[cfg(test)] mod tests block' method and got ~1047, over the ceiling; this approximation is wrong because several #[cfg(test)]-gated helper blocks are scattered through the file (lines 18/48/131/142/649) in addition to the trailing test module, which the naive method misses but the real classifier correctly excludes. arch-ctm's cited figure (852) is confirmed correct. Separately confirmed and flagged as a real but non-blocking tooling gap: .just/check_line_counts.py's collect_file_counts() only globs <crate_root>/src/**/*.rs; bin_support/ is a sibling of src/ and is never scanned, so the script's workspace-wide PASS never actually covered this file (req-qa traced this to the scanner source; crates/atm-daemon/src/daemon_observability.rs is a 1-line include!() shim pulling in the real bin_support/ file). This blind spot did not produce a wrong RULE-003 verdict this round only because the true count happens to be compliant -- recommend a follow-up to extend the scanner to scan bin_support/ or relocate the file under src/, tracked separately, not blocking this closure." .